!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-own-data.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/38/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/38/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  A kind is judged by where a base kind is defined, never by its spelling ([TSON-SCHEMA] §4.1): this schema
  declares a record of its own called `data`, which is not the meta-kernel's base kind, so `payload`
  composing it is an ordinary record -- a PRODUCT -- and a type a position may name.
  """
{
  data => {
    x: text
  }

  payload => data & {
    y: int32
  }

  holder => {
    p: payload
  }
}
